        "passage": "Table 3 summarises retrieval accuracy on in-domain and shifted test sets. Combining BM25 with the dense retriever improves top-20 accuracy over the dense-only baseline on both Natural Questions (+3.6) and TriviaQA (+2.9), with the largest gains on the shifted BEIR subsets. We attribute most of this gain to lexical matching of rare entity names that the dense encoder under-represents.",
